---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const PLAY_STORE = 'https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.eremat.greengains';
---

<Layout title="GreenGains — See your streets like you never have">
  <Nav />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative flex min-h-screen flex-col items-center justify-center px-6 pt-24 text-center">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_80%_50%_at_50%_-10%,rgba(16,185,129,0.10),transparent)]" />

    <h1 class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-5xl font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight md:text-7xl">
      See your commute<br />
      <span class="text-primary">differently.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="mx-auto mt-7 max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Every route you walk or drive, your phone reads the street.
      How bright it is. How rough. How it feels.
      GreenGains turns that into a map only you could have built.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
      <a
        href={PLAY_STORE}
        target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
      >
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3.18 23.76a2 2 0 0 0 2.84-.02l.05-.05 10.14-10.14-2.83-2.83L3.18 20.87a2 2 0 0 0 0 2.89ZM20.47 9.39l-2.75-1.57-3.18 3.18 3.18 3.18 2.76-1.58a2 2 0 0 0 0-3.21ZM2.01 1.05a2 2 0 0 0-.01 2.72L13.38 15.1l2.83-2.83L4.85 1.06A2 2 0 0 0 2.01 1.05Zm5.17 11.45L2.01 17.67v.01a2 2 0 0 0 2.84 2.83l5.29-5.29-2.96-2.72Z"/>
        </svg>
        Get the app — free
      </a>
      <a
        href="/dashboard/#map"
        class="rounded-lg border border-border px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:border-primary/60"
      >
        See the live map
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-xs text-muted">Android. Free. No account needed to see the map.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="border-t border-border">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-px md:grid-cols-3" style="background:theme('colors.border')">
      <div class="bg-bg px-8 py-10">
        <p class="font-semibold text-white">Install once. Forget about it.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">It runs in the background while you commute, walk, cycle. You don't need to open it. You won't think about it most days.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg px-8 py-10">
        <p class="font-semibold text-white">Your routes, not city averages.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">The map is yours. Your actual streets at your actual hours. Nobody else sees the same picture — because nobody else takes your exact routes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg px-8 py-10">
        <p class="font-semibold text-white">You're building something real.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Every route you map adds to a picture of the city that no satellite or city inspector can build. Just people going about their day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What you'll discover -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-28">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold md:text-4xl">What you'll find out about your streets.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Questions you never thought to ask — answered by sensors that have been on your phone for years.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 h-1.5 w-10 rounded-full bg-light" />
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-light">How bright is your street at night?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Some blocks are lit like daytime at 2am. Others go completely dark.
          GreenGains maps light levels at street level — from someone actually walking there, not a satellite.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 h-1.5 w-10 rounded-full bg-movement" />
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-movement">How rough is your commute, really?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          That one stretch of road you always dread? Your phone already knows exactly why.
          Potholes, patched tarmac, cobblestones — it registers everything as you ride.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 h-1.5 w-10 rounded-full bg-pressure" />
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-pressure">How does the pressure shift on your walk?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The air pressure changes as you move between streets, buildings, open spaces.
          Continuous readings at your level — not from a weather station miles away.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 h-1.5 w-10 rounded-full bg-quality" />
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-quality">What does your neighborhood's flow look like?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The rhythm of stops, the stillness at a crossing, the pace of a pedestrian street.
          Not your speed — the actual feel of moving through that place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 h-1.5 w-10 rounded-full" style="background:#a78bfa" />
        <h3 class="font-semibold" style="color:#a78bfa">What's underneath your street?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Power lines, subway infrastructure, transformer stations — they all leave a magnetic signature.
          Your phone's compass reads it as you pass. Most people have no idea it's there.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-7 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="mb-5 h-1.5 w-10 rounded-full bg-primary/40" />
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-muted">More coming</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
            Humidity, UV, cellular signal — sensors already on most devices.
            We add them when the data is worth collecting.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Map section -->
  <section id="map" class="border-y border-border bg-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between">
        <div class="max-w-lg">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">The map</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold md:text-4xl">A map nobody else could make.</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Every hex is a real place mapped by a real person.
            No drones. No fieldwork. No city contracts.
            Just people going about their day — and the streets they actually live on.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
            The more people map an area, the sharper the picture.
            Right now it's sparse in places. That's honest.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/dashboard/#map"
            class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:border-primary/60"
          >
            Open the live map
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
              <path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:w-64">
          {[
            { n: '~174m', label: 'Resolution of your personal map' },
            { n: '5', label: 'Sensors reading as you move' },
            { n: '0', label: 'Things you need to do to collect data' },
          ].map(s => (
            <div class="border-l-2 border-primary/30 pl-4">
              <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary">{s.n}</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">{s.label}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-t border-border px-6 py-28 text-center">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_80%_at_50%_100%,rgba(16,185,129,0.07),transparent)]" />
    <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold md:text-5xl">Start seeing your streets.</h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-sm text-muted">
      Android. Free. Nothing to set up.
    </p>
    <a
      href={PLAY_STORE}
      target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="mt-9 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-primary px-8 py-3.5 font-semibold text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
    >
      Get on Android
    </a>
    <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-muted">
      Working with a municipality or research team?
      <a href="/business" class="text-primary/70 hover:text-primary transition-colors">See the data API →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
